It's also our case.

230
00:10:41.875 --> 00:10:45.505
Yeah. we just signed on as legal
consultants to the defense just now.

231
00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:50.039
And you will sell your little sideshow
act to anyone who'll listen. won't you?

232
00:10:50.116 --> 00:10:52.381
Just don't screw this one up.

233
00:10:53.286 --> 00:10:55.778
"Don't screw this up"?

234
00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:59.357
Hey. Lassy. that really
wasn't much of a put down.

235
00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:02.691
In fact it was
somewhat inspiring.

236
00:11:03.563 --> 00:11:05.623
Las. let's roll that back!

237
00:11:09.836 --> 00:11:12.533
I don't know. It
feels a little weird.

238
00:11:12.939 --> 00:11:15.602
I mean. you should really be
sitting here. This is your office.

239
00:11:15.675 --> 00:11:17.644
Yeah. this isn't my office.

240
00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:21.442
You didn't like mine. This is Carter
Jarecki's office. one of the partners.

241
00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:24.643
Actually. he's the guy who
took the case in the first place.

242
00:11:24.717 --> 00:11:27.744
but then dumped it on me when
he decided it was a lost cause.

243
00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:29.846
You see. that's exactly
what I'm talking about.

244
00:11:29.923 --> 00:11:31.653
Why didn't you
stand up to that guy?

245
00:11:31.724 --> 00:11:35.491
For the worst reason possible. I
actually believe this woman is innocent.

246
00:11:35.562 --> 00:11:38.726
Now. can we please go
before Jarecki gets back?

247
00:11:41.201 --> 00:11:46.162
Carter Jarecki just left for a nooner with
his mistress. We have at least two hours.

248
00:11:50.743 --> 00:11:52.336
Maybe an hour and a half.

249
00:11:52.412 --> 00:11:55.382
Hornstock. I think you have the
potential to be a fantastic lawyer.

250
00:11:55.448 --> 00:11:59.180
You just need confidence. After all.
that's your name on the door. Now come on!

251
00:11:59.252 --> 00:12:02.689
Oh. no. No. None of
those Hornstocks are me.

252
00:12:02.755 --> 00:12:06.385
The first one is my
grandfather. he founded the firm.

253
00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:09.827
The other one is my
father. then my brother.

254
00:12:09.896 --> 00:12:11.728
Wow. A whole family of lawyers?

255
00:12:11.798 --> 00:12:13.733
Yeah. even my sister.

256
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.395
Well. there you go.
She didn't make the door.

257
00:12:16.469 --> 00:12:19.405
She's Biederman.
It's her married name.

258
00:12:21.274 --> 00:12:23.352
Well. we're gonna need to
take a look at your witness list

259
00:12:23.376 --> 00:12:24.810
and your deposition transcripts.

260
00:12:24.877 --> 00:12:27.142
Oh. yeah. Well. I
prepared all that for you.

261
00:12:27.213 --> 00:12:30.650
I have... Here are all the
forensic and arrest reports.

262
00:12:30.717 --> 00:12:34.484
And I deposed several of
Hale's coworkers from Channel 8.

263
00:12:34.554 --> 00:12:37.991
mostly to refute timelines
and for character testimony.

264
00:12:38.057 --> 00:12:39.184
Can we see those?

265
00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:41.251
Oh. sure. yeah. It's...

266
00:12:44.464 --> 00:12:45.796
Oh. yes.

267
00:12:45.865 --> 00:12:48.801
And maybe. later on we can
read the phonebook. just for fun.

268
00:12:48.868 --> 00:12:53.169
Hornstock. I've
gotta do what I do.

269
00:12:53.539 --> 00:12:55.167
That's not the way I do it.

270
00:12:55.241 --> 00:12:58.405
I need to see. feel
and smell people

271
00:12:58.478 --> 00:13:00.640
in order to figure
out what happens.

272
00:13:00.847 --> 00:13:02.110
Smell them?

273
00:13:04.117 --> 00:13:07.884
So. this is where the...
The crime took place.

274
00:13:07.954 --> 00:13:09.889
So. just feel free to
have a look around.

275
00:13:09.956 --> 00:13:12.824
and do whatever it is you do.

276
00:13:12.892 --> 00:13:14.326
Okay. Thank you.

277
00:13:18.231 --> 00:13:20.666
Let's walk the crime.
shall we? Yeah.

278
00:13:20.733 --> 00:13:23.635
He probably came in from that
same entrance we did. Right.

279
00:13:23.703 --> 00:13:28.801
Found their way over here to
the Channel 8 anchor desk area.

280
00:13:28.875 --> 00:13:32.676
Of course. the body
was found here.

281
00:13:34.047 --> 00:13:35.879
It was a short walk. Yeah.

282
00:13:35.948 --> 00:13:38.281
Priscilla. what are
these green walls for?

283
00:13:38.351 --> 00:13:40.115
Oh. well we do it
all on green screen.

284
00:13:40.186 --> 00:13:42.587
Really? Can you show
me how that works. please?

285
00:13:42.655 --> 00:13:45.352
Sure. I just need
someone to sit in front.

286
00:13:45.425 --> 00:13:46.893
Gus. go sit over there.

287
00:13:46.959 --> 00:13:49.793
I'm not going to sit there just
'cause you tell me to. Shawn.

288
00:13:49.862 --> 00:13:51.854
Fine. I'll... I'll
play anchorman.

289
00:13:51.931 --> 00:13:53.729
I got it. I got it.

290
00:13:57.804 --> 00:14:01.935
Okay. so we've just have to go to
the control room. It's just this way.

291
00:14:02.008 --> 00:14:03.067
Okay.

292
00:14:05.078 --> 00:14:06.876
You know when we're
watching the weather guy.

293
00:14:06.946 --> 00:14:09.609
and it looks like he's got.
like. rainfall behind him? Yeah.

294
00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:11.241
Or snow or hail? Yeah.

295
00:14:11.317 --> 00:14:13.128
How does that work? Well.
the green background works

296
00:14:13.152 --> 00:14:16.122
as a blank slate. Then I
just run it through the board

297
00:14:16.723 --> 00:14:18.385
and presto!

298
00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:21.158
A composite of the
two images is made.

299
00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:22.695
Oh. oh! Can we
get sound in here?

300
00:14:22.762 --> 00:14:24.253
Yeah. yeah. Sure.

301
00:14:25.431 --> 00:14:26.455
<i>In local news.</i>

302
00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:28.660
<i>a pharmaceutical
representative again provided</i>

303
00:14:28.735 --> 00:14:32.035
<i>the key piece of information
in a baffling police case.</i>

304
00:14:32.105 --> 00:14:34.040
But ran screaming
from the scene.

305
00:14:34.107 --> 00:14:37.168
like a little girl before he
could make a statement.

306
00:14:37.243 --> 00:14:39.872
That was one time. Shawn!
One time! I don't like dead bodies!

307
00:14:39.946 --> 00:14:42.472
I told you that. Now
stop bringing that up!

308
00:14:44.217 --> 00:14:46.914
Hello. this is your local news.

309
00:14:48.654 --> 00:14:50.418
This next office
was Jackson Hale's.

310
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.568
I've got to tell you guys.
everybody's been acting a little weird

311
00:14:52.592 --> 00:14:55.061
since it happened.
It's just not the same.

312
00:14:55.194 --> 00:14:59.495
Oh! Ruben. this is Shawn
Spencer and Burton Guster.

313
00:14:59.565 --> 00:15:01.431
They're working on
Jackson Hale's case.

314
00:15:01.501 --> 00:15:04.403
This is Ruben Leonard. he's a lab
meteorologist on Jackson's team.

315
00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:05.597
Was.

316
00:15:06.706 --> 00:15:09.699
I was just sorting and packing

317
00:15:09.776 --> 00:15:13.713
some of his more important
things to send to his family.

318
00:15:14.113 --> 00:15:15.376
It's the least I can do.

319
00:15:15.448 --> 00:15:16.541
That's very thoughtful.

320
00:15:16.616 --> 00:15:17.675
Thank you.

321
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.862
<i>That reminds me of a hot.
little</i> señorita <i>I met there.</i>

322
00:15:19.886 --> 00:15:21.354
<i>She was serving
fried jalapenos...</i>

323
00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:22.650
Would you excuse me? Sure.

324
00:15:22.722 --> 00:15:23.883
Sure. Thanks.

325
00:15:25.358 --> 00:15:26.883
<i>So. if you'll notice that...</i>

326
00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:28.170
Did you work with
Jackson Hale long?

327
00:15:28.194 --> 00:15:31.392
Six years. He was a great man.

328
00:15:32.865 --> 00:15:34.925
I had a lot of respect for him.

329
00:15:39.505 --> 00:15:41.133
He was just so
good at what he did.

330
00:15:41.207 --> 00:15:43.005
<i>Take your umbrella
because I guarantee.</i>

331
00:15:43.075 --> 00:15:45.635
<i>it's raining cats
and dogs out there.</i>

332
00:15:45.711 --> 00:15:47.509
A broadcasting treasure.

333
00:15:48.648 --> 00:15:51.743
<i>Anyway. take a look
at Thursday here...</i>

334
00:15:55.555 --> 00:15:57.046
Dude.

335
00:15:58.324 --> 00:16:00.418
Ruben's in there
destroying Hale's awards.

336
00:16:00.493 --> 00:16:01.552
What? Yeah.

337
00:16:01.627 --> 00:16:04.426
Unless he's really offended by
the shoddy engraving on the plaque.

338
00:16:04.497 --> 00:16:10.334
that guy hates Jackson Hale. I'm not saying
he did it. but reasonable doubt. anyone?

339
00:16:15.208 --> 00:16:19.270
Okay. Miss Panitch. Please. walk
us through the night of the crime.

340
00:16:20.012 --> 00:16:23.574
Well. I never met
Mr. Hale before that night.

341
00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:25.880
I just moved here
from Wisconsin.

342
00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:27.351
It wasn't like I
was a fan of his.

343
00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:29.980
I only vaguely knew
he was a weatherman.

344
00:16:30.189 --> 00:16:33.216
So we talked. and
he was charming...

345
00:16:33.292 --> 00:16:34.817
So the scratches on
Jackson Hale's back

346
00:16:34.894 --> 00:16:36.487
and his skin under
your fingernails.

347
00:16:36.562 --> 00:16:38.292
this all happened
during the sex.

348
00:16:38.364 --> 00:16:40.299
as well as the
bruises on your arm?

349
00:16:40.366 --> 00:16:42.494
It got passionate.

350
00:16:42.568 --> 00:16:45.299
I don't remember anything
until I woke up the next morning.

351
00:16:45.371 --> 00:16:46.634
With his blood on you?

352
00:16:46.706 --> 00:16:48.116
And then you fled
to the parking lot?

353
00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.371
Look. I was scared.

354
00:16:50.443 --> 00:16:54.175
I. I know how bad
all of this looks. I do.

355
00:16:54.247 --> 00:16:58.207
But I swear I did
not murder anyone.

356
00:16:58.284 --> 00:17:01.448
Do you guys believe me? Do you?

357
00:17:01.587 --> 00:17:04.182
Of course we do.
Sandra. Don't be ridiculous.

358
00:17:04.257 --> 00:17:05.555
Counselor? Yes?

359
00:17:05.625 --> 00:17:07.269
Would you please retire
with me to the hallway.

360
00:17:07.293 --> 00:17:10.229
where we can exchange
words in hushed tones?

361
00:17:13.065 --> 00:17:14.727
Okay. what are you doing? What?

362
00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.929
You are supposed to be demonstrating
confidence and swagger for Hornstock.

363
00:17:18.004 --> 00:17:20.616
Instead you're poking holes in our
case. and you're scaring our defendant.

364
00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.701
Here are the facts. Shawn. All we
know about Sandra is what she's told us.

365
00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:25.438
I think we need to
do some investigating.

366
00:17:25.511 --> 00:17:27.856
I believe her. Hornstock believes
her. What else do we need?

367
00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.371
We need proof. Shawn.

368
00:17:29.448 --> 00:17:30.848
Look. right here in this book?

369
00:17:30.917 --> 00:17:35.912
<i>Corey v. Bulevic</i> in 1955. The key piece
of evidence were half-melted candlesticks.

370
00:17:35.988 --> 00:17:38.355
We need evidence! Where
are our candlesticks. Shawn?

371
00:17:38.424 --> 00:17:39.756
Maybe you just jumped over them?

372
00:17:39.825 --> 00:17:41.851
What? Be nimble. Be quick.

373
00:17:41.928 --> 00:17:43.505
You're not going to give
me anything for that?

374
00:17:43.529 --> 00:17:45.088
Now can we please...

375
00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.597
Whoa. whoa. whoa!
Check out the judge.

376
00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:52.866
He's grabbing his back.
No wonder he's so grumpy.

377
00:17:52.939 --> 00:17:55.059
He's not grabbing his back.
he's grabbing his kidneys.

378
00:17:55.107 --> 00:17:57.042
He probably has a kidney stone.

379
00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.469
Dude. nice! Thank you.

380
00:18:00.046 --> 00:18:04.006
Please state to the court what
your relationship with Mr. Hale was.

381
00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:07.645
It was professional. He was
my boss. I was his receptionist.

382
00:18:08.154 --> 00:18:11.181
And as the Channel 8
receptionist. Miss Osterman.

383
00:18:11.257 --> 00:18:15.627
if people were to call Jackson
Hale. you took those calls?

384
00:18:15.695 --> 00:18:16.695
I did.

385
00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:21.894
And did you receive any calls from the
defendant. Sandra Panitch. at any time?

386
00:18:21.968 --> 00:18:23.459
Oh. not to my knowledge. No.

387
00:18:23.536 --> 00:18:25.437
But other women would call?

388
00:18:25.504 --> 00:18:26.597
Sure.

389
00:18:26.672 --> 00:18:29.039
Was Jackson Hale
sleeping with these women?

390
00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:31.270
Objection. Your Honor. hearsay.

391
00:18:31.444 --> 00:18:32.810
I'll allow the question.

392
00:18:32.878 --> 00:18:35.848
Well. I can only say
that I fielded many calls.

393
00:18:35.915 --> 00:18:39.113
and sometimes I helped
to juggle these calls.

394
00:18:39.185 --> 00:18:40.585
He was a handsome man.

395
00:18:40.653 --> 00:18:42.645
He certainly was.

396
00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:47.851
Thank you. Miss Osterman.

397
00:18:47.927 --> 00:18:50.158
You may step down.
Miss Osterman.

398
00:18:50.229 --> 00:18:51.229
Thanks.

399
00:18:51.597 --> 00:18:55.967
Your Honor. the state requests a
moment to prepare for our next witness.

400
00:18:56.035 --> 00:18:58.266
"He certainly was"? What
happened? You were rolling!

401
00:18:58.337 --> 00:19:01.034
I don't know. I don't know.
it sounded good in my head.

402
00:19:01.107 --> 00:19:02.769
You have a great
support system. you know.

403
00:19:02.842 --> 00:19:03.919
it gives you that
easy confidence.

404
00:19:03.943 --> 00:19:05.954
But. you know. my father hasn't
been in the courtroom once.

405
00:19:05.978 --> 00:19:07.002
Not one of my trials.

406
00:19:07.079 --> 00:19:09.191
You've been here one day.
and your father's already here.

407
00:19:09.215 --> 00:19:10.774
What are you talking about?

408
00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:13.547
Oh. I met him outside.
He's a really nice guy.

409
00:19:22.094 --> 00:19:25.462
Your Honor. the defense
would like to call for a recess.

410
00:19:25.531 --> 00:19:27.557
Excuse me. Who are you?

411
00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:30.193
I'm sorry. Your Honor. My
name is Shawn Spencer.

412
00:19:30.269 --> 00:19:31.913
I'm a psychic legal
consultant on this case.

413
00:19:31.937 --> 00:19:35.704
Objection. Your Honor. We were not made
aware that a psychic was hired on this case.

414
00:19:35.775 --> 00:19:38.074
Approach the bench. all of you.

415
00:19:38.411 --> 00:19:39.411
Sweet.

416
00:19:42.415 --> 00:19:44.179
Your Honor. the people
question his validity.

417
00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.776
Okay. first of
all. that's hurtful.

418
00:19:46.852 --> 00:19:48.514
Look. I know you're
the big bad prosecutor

419
00:19:48.587 --> 00:19:51.216
with the sweet head. but is
this tone really necessary?

420
00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.225
No. Look. I'm a
legitimate consultant.

421
00:19:53.292 --> 00:19:55.671
I've been hired often by the
Santa Barbara Police Department.

422
00:19:55.695 --> 00:19:59.564
and there is a high-ranking detective
in this very courtroom right now.

423
00:19:59.632 --> 00:20:01.999
who will vouch for my validity.

424
00:20:02.068 --> 00:20:03.730
And who is this?

425
00:20:03.803 --> 00:20:07.171
He's right there. The wispy.
yet commanding Irish fellow.

426
00:20:07.239 --> 00:20:09.640
who looks like he's been
sucking on the Sour Patch Kids.

427
00:20:09.709 --> 00:20:12.770
Will you stand and state
your name for the court?

428
00:20:13.779 --> 00:20:16.613
Carlton Lassiter. Santa Barbara
Police Department. Your Honor.

429
00:20:16.682 --> 00:20:19.982
Head detective.
11 years this May.

430
00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:23.614
Perhaps you'd like to inform the
court of your favorite color as well.

431
00:20:23.689 --> 00:20:25.783
The point is. do
you know this man?

432
00:20:25.858 --> 00:20:26.882
I do.

433
00:20:26.959 --> 00:20:29.554
And has he worked on
cases for the department?

434
00:20:29.628 --> 00:20:30.926
He has.

435
00:20:30.996 --> 00:20:32.274
There you have it.
There you have it.

436
00:20:32.298 --> 00:20:33.766
And he was helpful?

437
00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:35.566
Absolutely.

438
00:20:38.537 --> 00:20:40.415
Did he just say absolutely
with a little half smile?

439
00:20:40.439 --> 00:20:41.550
I'd like that
printed out. please.

440
00:20:41.574 --> 00:20:45.477
I'm thinking of shellacking it on a nice
piece of maple. maybe a little decoupage.

441
00:20:45.544 --> 00:20:47.308
Your Honor. as you
can see. I'm responsible

442
00:20:47.379 --> 00:20:49.678
for breaking many cases
here in the state of California.

443
00:20:49.749 --> 00:20:54.119
Well. guess what? I don't care who
you are. or what you've done for the state.

444
00:20:54.186 --> 00:20:58.282
I don't believe in that psychic mumbo-jumbo
and it's not welcome in my court!

445
00:20:58.357 --> 00:20:59.416
"Mumbo-jumbo"?

446
00:20:59.492 --> 00:21:02.985
Oh! You poor. poor man.

447
00:21:03.162 --> 00:21:04.960
No wonder. You're...

448
00:21:05.498 --> 00:21:08.093
Passing a kidney stone
can be very stressful.

449
00:21:08.167 --> 00:21:10.102
Who told you that?
I never told anyone.

450
00:21:10.169 --> 00:21:12.661
You tell me if I'm
overstepping my bounds here.

451
00:21:12.738 --> 00:21:16.004
but I'd like to suggest an old home remedy
that did wonders for my Aunt Dolores.

452
00:21:16.075 --> 00:21:18.101
She simply gargled
with some mineral water.

453
00:21:18.177 --> 00:21:19.454
followed it up with
some raw greens.

454
00:21:19.478 --> 00:21:21.447
Me. personally. I'd
go with asparagus tips.

455
00:21:21.514 --> 00:21:25.781
that way. later on. when
you're making water.

456
00:21:26.952 --> 00:21:28.716
you'll know that it's working.

457
00:21:32.825 --> 00:21:34.293
Let's proceed with the trial.

458
00:21:37.062 --> 00:21:39.293
Okay. you got me? I'm startled.
What are you doing here?

459
00:21:39.365 --> 00:21:40.731
Well. maybe we're both psychics.

460
00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.325
I am serious.

461
00:21:42.401 --> 00:21:44.802
Occasionally. I come
down here. I sit in on a trial.

462
00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.600
Today. I get a phone call.

463
00:21:46.672 --> 00:21:48.538
Guess who's practicing law now?

464
00:21:48.607 --> 00:21:50.872
Wait a minute. You
come down here regularly?

465
00:21:50.943 --> 00:21:53.708
Thursdays. usually.
Today was just a bonus.

466
00:21:53.779 --> 00:21:56.840
My God. you just
can't let go. can you?

467
00:21:57.449 --> 00:22:00.977
You retired too early. Not my fault. I
didn't ask you to turn in your badge. Dad.

468
00:22:01.053 --> 00:22:03.373
Shawn! Shawn! Shawn! I'm in
there trying to do something...

469
00:22:03.422 --> 00:22:07.154
You seem to forget whose name you've
got at the end of your letterhead. kid.

470
00:22:07.226 --> 00:22:10.355
When you use my name.
it is my business as well.

471
00:22:11.163 --> 00:22:12.825
Give me my phone.

472
00:22:15.568 --> 00:22:18.163
Took you long enough to
figure out the kidney stone.

473
00:22:19.271 --> 00:22:24.835
Let it be noted that the witness
identified the defendant. Sandra Panitch.

474
00:22:25.077 --> 00:22:30.072
as the woman he saw running through
the parking lot on the night of the murder.

475
00:22:31.116 --> 00:22:32.641
Has it been authenticated?

476
00:22:32.718 --> 00:22:35.313
Hey. what would Phelps
need to get authenticated?

477
00:22:35.387 --> 00:22:36.821
I don't know.

478
00:22:36.889 --> 00:22:39.449
His little collection
of green army men?

479
00:22:39.525 --> 00:22:41.721
H-Stock. did you
just make a joke?

480
00:22:41.794 --> 00:22:43.228
Hmm? I think you did.

481
00:22:44.363 --> 00:22:47.629
Your witness. Does the
defense wish to cross-examine?

482
00:22:49.268 --> 00:22:51.100
Your Honor. the defense rests.

483
00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:53.730
No. No. it doesn't.

484
00:22:55.574 --> 00:22:59.204
Your Honor. the defense
may rest. Why am I not resting?

485
00:22:59.278 --> 00:23:00.803
I have a vibe
that's very strong.

486
00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:04.248
Hatred. jealousy. That guy
wanted to be a serious weatherman.

487
00:23:04.316 --> 00:23:06.945
He has no sympathy for
Jackson Hale whatsoever.

488
00:23:07.019 --> 00:23:08.885
Wait. What? You think he did it?

489
00:23:08.954 --> 00:23:11.014
No. I'm pretty sure he didn't.

490
00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:13.286
But we can plant a seed.

491
00:23:13.359 --> 00:23:15.260
Johnny Applestock.

492
00:23:15.327 --> 00:23:18.991
Your Honor. the
defense does not rest.

493
00:23:23.168 --> 00:23:27.765
Mr. Leonard. you are a
meteorologist. are you not?

494
00:23:28.641 --> 00:23:30.337
Yes. I am indeed.

495
00:23:30.509 --> 00:23:32.171
But not on the air?

496
00:23:32.878 --> 00:23:34.676
No. not on the air.

497
00:23:34.747 --> 00:23:39.811
Hmm. Maybe because you
don't have a meteorologist name.

498
00:23:39.885 --> 00:23:41.251
I don't follow.

499
00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:43.289
Well. correct me if I'm wrong.

500
00:23:43.355 --> 00:23:48.020
but Leonard isn't a term
for any kind of weather?

501
00:23:48.827 --> 00:23:49.886
No. it is not.

502
00:23:49.962 --> 00:23:54.263
So. if I was to look up Leonard.
in say. a weather glossary.

503
00:23:54.333 --> 00:23:55.562
there would be no definition?

504
00:23:55.634 --> 00:23:57.159
No. there would not.

505
00:23:57.236 --> 00:23:59.262
Excuse me. where is this going?

506
00:23:59.338 --> 00:24:02.069
Yes. Mr. Hornstock. where
are you going with this?

507
00:24:02.141 --> 00:24:06.135
I'm sorry. Your Honor. it's just
that every successful weatherman

508
00:24:06.211 --> 00:24:09.511
that I know of. has a
real weatherman's name.

509
00:24:09.581 --> 00:24:12.745
Johnny Mountain. Dallas Rains?

510
00:24:13.319 --> 00:24:15.481
Oh. Jackson Hale. for example.

511
00:24:15.554 --> 00:24:17.648
Hey. first of all that
wasn't even his real name.

512
00:24:17.723 --> 00:24:18.918
Precisely.

513
00:24:18.991 --> 00:24:21.620
Have you ever considered going
by the name of Bolt Lightning?

514
00:24:21.694 --> 00:24:22.821
No.

515
00:24:25.097 --> 00:24:27.191
Cloudy McMillen? No.

516
00:24:27.333 --> 00:24:28.858
Wendy Morning Dew?

517
00:24:28.968 --> 00:24:32.132
That's a woman's name.
Okay. look. I have a degree

518
00:24:32.204 --> 00:24:34.969
in meteorology from
the University of Virginia.

519
00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:37.566
I wrote my thesis on
Bernoulli's theorem

520
00:24:37.643 --> 00:24:39.271
of incompressible level flow.

521
00:24:39.345 --> 00:24:43.715
and I was a junior tornado
safety captain for seven years.

522
00:24:43.782 --> 00:24:46.217
Jackson Hale has
a degree in what?

523
00:24:46.418 --> 00:24:49.047
Physical education
from a junior college.

524
00:24:49.121 --> 00:24:51.647
He was an embarrassment.
He was worthless. all right?

525
00:24:51.724 --> 00:24:55.320
He was worthless to anyone who
was a real meteorologist like myself.

526
00:24:55.394 --> 00:24:59.195
He should have been
stabbed in the heart long ago!

527
00:24:59.264 --> 00:25:01.062
Objection. Your Honor.

528
00:25:03.168 --> 00:25:06.195
It's a little late for that.
don't you think. Counselor?

529
00:25:06.271 --> 00:25:08.016
That's the kind of
confidence I'm talking about.

530
00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:09.117
That's what I'm talking about.

531
00:25:09.141 --> 00:25:11.269
We are on our way
to winning this thing.

532
00:25:15.047 --> 00:25:18.142
Told you. She's kind
and she's innocent.

533
00:25:18.217 --> 00:25:20.228
Just because we had a
small victory in court yesterday

534
00:25:20.252 --> 00:25:21.496
doesn't mean we're
out of the woods.

535
00:25:21.520 --> 00:25:22.818
Son of a bitch!

536
00:25:23.022 --> 00:25:25.100
Alligator pumps! I swear. I
should arrest that weatherman.

537
00:25:25.124 --> 00:25:27.491
He clearly stated it was
not going to rain today.

538
00:25:27.559 --> 00:25:31.553
You see. that's the problem with
what I like to call "group thinking."

539
00:25:31.630 --> 00:25:32.741
We don't listen
to group thinkers.

540
00:25:32.765 --> 00:25:33.765
Nope.

541
00:25:33.832 --> 00:25:35.076
In fact. we don't listen
to weathermen at all.

542
00:25:35.100 --> 00:25:38.502
If you excuse me. I've
really got better things to do.

543
00:25:38.971 --> 00:25:40.940
Dinner with your cat?

544
00:25:41.473 --> 00:25:42.805
O'Hara. are you coming?

545
00:25:42.875 --> 00:25:44.673
You go. I'll catch
up with you in a sec.

546
00:25:44.743 --> 00:25:46.712
You know. Shawn. for a psychic.

547
00:25:46.779 --> 00:25:50.375
you are missing something right
in front of your face. It's too bad.

548
00:25:50.449 --> 00:25:53.361
You might actually learn something
about Lassiter. Maybe you don't want to.

549
00:25:53.385 --> 00:25:55.013
He waxes his back?

550
00:25:55.087 --> 00:25:56.146
I'm gonna go now.

551
00:25:56.221 --> 00:25:59.919
Shawn. I don't care what anyone
else says. The pink shirt is working.

552
00:26:11.570 --> 00:26:12.629
Okay. that was cryptic.

553
00:26:12.704 --> 00:26:14.536
Not really. I'll be damned.

554
00:26:28.454 --> 00:26:29.547
Who's Detective Assi?

555
00:26:29.621 --> 00:26:33.752
Lassy. It's Lassiter. He must have
sent some sort of memo to Phelps.

556
00:26:33.826 --> 00:26:36.193
The question is
why would Lassiter

557
00:26:36.261 --> 00:26:38.196
send a letter to
the D.A.'s office?

558
00:26:38.263 --> 00:26:40.027
Don't you ever
watch <i>Law and Order?</i>

559
00:26:40.099 --> 00:26:42.762
They tend to work
together sometimes.

560
00:26:42.835 --> 00:26:45.771
Right. So... So. go
ahead and check the files.

561
00:26:45.838 --> 00:26:47.397
and find me that letter.

562
00:26:47.473 --> 00:26:48.839
Phelps received
it on the seventh.

563
00:26:48.907 --> 00:26:49.984
I've been through all of them.

564
00:26:50.008 --> 00:26:52.353
There are no memos submitted
into evidence. filed on the seventh.

565
00:26:52.377 --> 00:26:55.176
So. it didn't get filed.
But there is a memo.

566
00:26:56.148 --> 00:26:59.414
So whatever's on that
memo is clearly worth hiding.

567
00:27:01.453 --> 00:27:03.684
And she told you this directly?

568
00:27:03.755 --> 00:27:05.747
Yes. when I questioned
the defendant.

569
00:27:05.824 --> 00:27:07.902
she admitted to having
sexual relations with the victim.

570
00:27:07.926 --> 00:27:10.919
But not to stabbing
him with a letter opener?

571
00:27:14.066 --> 00:27:18.026
Well. she appeared at the time to
be confused and had memory gaps.

572
00:27:18.103 --> 00:27:20.629
She claimed never to have
seen or touched the weapon.

573
00:27:20.706 --> 00:27:24.404
Even though her fingerprints
were all over it. I see.

574
00:27:25.911 --> 00:27:28.904
Thank you. Detective
Lassiter. Nothing further.

575
00:27:29.615 --> 00:27:30.776
Your witness.

576
00:27:30.849 --> 00:27:31.849
You sure about this?

577
00:27:31.917 --> 00:27:34.443
Yes. I have a very strong
feeling about this letter.

578
00:27:34.520 --> 00:27:37.581
First rule of trial law. never ask a
question you don't know the answer to.

579
00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:41.320
Hey. have I steered
you wrong yet? Come on.

580
00:27:42.961 --> 00:27:47.092
Detective Lassiter.
did you send a letter

581
00:27:47.166 --> 00:27:50.193
to the D.A.'s office on
the seventh of August?

582
00:27:51.570 --> 00:27:52.936
Yes. I did.

583
00:27:53.005 --> 00:27:54.496
And what did it say?

584
00:27:54.573 --> 00:27:56.701
I... Objection.
lack of foundation.

585
00:27:57.276 --> 00:28:00.371
I'll allow it. Go ahead.
tell the jury what it said.

586
00:28:00.445 --> 00:28:03.540
It questioned the
defendant's motive.

587
00:28:03.615 --> 00:28:05.811
That it was very
strong. you mean?

588
00:28:05.884 --> 00:28:08.718
No. it questioned whether I
believed the defendant had one at all.

589
00:28:10.122 --> 00:28:13.217
The prosecution never
submitted this letter into evidence.

590
00:28:13.292 --> 00:28:16.626
So. at this point. Your Honor.
the defense calls for a mistrial.

591
00:28:20.132 --> 00:28:21.498
Man. this is fun!

592
00:28:21.567 --> 00:28:23.092
Approach the bench.

593
00:28:25.237 --> 00:28:28.867
We may have received
the letter. I... I can't be sure.

594
00:28:28.974 --> 00:28:31.341
We didn't knowingly withhold it.

595
00:28:31.410 --> 00:28:33.311
My office is wall
to wall papers.

596
00:28:33.378 --> 00:28:36.644
Then go to Staples and buy
yourself some new file folders.

597
00:28:36.715 --> 00:28:39.150
but until then. you are warned.

598
00:28:39.218 --> 00:28:43.246
Any new evidence must be
submitted to all parties immediately.

599
00:28:43.322 --> 00:28:45.223
Do I make myself clear?

600
00:28:45.290 --> 00:28:46.952
Yes. Your Honor.

601
00:28:47.025 --> 00:28:49.256
And in the spirit
of that ruling.

602
00:28:49.328 --> 00:28:51.524
I would like to submit a
new piece of evidence.

603
00:28:51.597 --> 00:28:55.625
If this is that willy-nilly piece of
evidence that you tried to get in.

604
00:28:55.701 --> 00:28:58.261
in pre-trial. I'll tell
you one more time.

605
00:28:58.337 --> 00:29:02.468
I will not admit any audio-visual
evidence unless it's been authenticated.

606
00:29:03.542 --> 00:29:05.022
<i>We're talking about
playing it to him.</i>

607
00:29:06.511 --> 00:29:07.511
It's a videotape.

608
00:29:07.579 --> 00:29:08.638
Hmm?

609
00:29:08.714 --> 00:29:11.684
We just got our authentication
papers from the lab in Sacramento.

610
00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:15.380
It is a videotape of the
defendant. Sandra Panitch.

611
00:29:15.454 --> 00:29:17.787
murdering the
victim. Jackson Hale.

612
00:29:29.101 --> 00:29:31.627
Judge. I argue that this
tape should not be admissible.

613
00:29:31.703 --> 00:29:32.762
On what grounds?

614
00:29:32.838 --> 00:29:36.002
Well. we're citing
unfair surprisery.

615
00:29:36.074 --> 00:29:38.839
I... I still don't understand
why he is in this room.

616
00:29:38.910 --> 00:29:40.538
He's nothing but a disruption.

617
00:29:40.612 --> 00:29:43.047
Maybe someday. Phelps.
when you're a judge.

618
00:29:43.115 --> 00:29:44.777
which I highly
doubt will happen.

619
00:29:44.850 --> 00:29:48.014
then you can decide who's
welcome in your chambers.

620
00:29:48.086 --> 00:29:51.545
Your Honor. these guys are a part
of my team. and I want them here.

621
00:29:51.623 --> 00:29:55.082
Why? You used to be a
good lawyer. Hornstock.

622
00:29:55.160 --> 00:29:58.995
But let's face it. if you've gotta
resort to hiring this idiot psychic

623
00:29:59.064 --> 00:30:00.157
and his little sidekick...

624
00:30:00.232 --> 00:30:01.376
I'm nobody's sidekick. you...

625
00:30:01.400 --> 00:30:02.766
Whoa! Gus. Gus. Come on.

626
00:30:02.834 --> 00:30:04.132
Forget you.

627
00:30:04.202 --> 00:30:07.969
Gus. we are all grown men
here. Let's just take a beat.

628
00:30:09.441 --> 00:30:11.876
Let's... Let's take a step back.

629
00:30:12.678 --> 00:30:14.237
Let's take a step back.

630
00:30:17.015 --> 00:30:20.144
Mr. Hornstock. having now
seen the video in question.

631
00:30:20.218 --> 00:30:23.120
I don't think I need to tell
you how damaging it is.

632
00:30:23.188 --> 00:30:24.679
I strongly suggest at this point

633
00:30:24.756 --> 00:30:28.090
that you consider accepting
a plea bargain for murder two.

634
00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:31.790
Your Honor. I will have to review
the tape and confer with my client.

635
00:30:31.863 --> 00:30:33.729
I tell you what. Hornstock.

636
00:30:33.799 --> 00:30:37.668
I will leave murder two on the
table until tomorrow morning.

637
00:30:37.736 --> 00:30:39.568
Consider that my gift to you.

638
00:30:46.745 --> 00:30:48.441
She doesn't realize
she's being taped.

639
00:30:48.513 --> 00:30:51.574
No. I don't think this is
his first barbeque either.

640
00:30:51.650 --> 00:30:53.448
if you know what I mean.

641
00:30:53.552 --> 00:30:56.579
This high-def plasma
really makes a difference.

642
00:30:56.655 --> 00:30:59.454
I see the beads of
sweat on his neck.

643
00:30:59.524 --> 00:31:00.753
Look at his hair!

644
00:31:00.826 --> 00:31:01.885
That's horrible!

645
00:31:03.061 --> 00:31:04.324
<i>Yeah.</i>

646
00:31:05.397 --> 00:31:06.592
<i>Oh. wow!</i>

647
00:31:07.799 --> 00:31:09.961
Do any of you make
noises like that?

648
00:31:11.436 --> 00:31:12.436
His or hers?

649
00:31:18.877 --> 00:31:23.110
When she sees this. she
will certainly take the deal.

650
00:31:24.649 --> 00:31:26.379
I'm not going to take the deal.

651
00:31:26.451 --> 00:31:28.896
If you don't take the deal. you
could go away possibly for life.

652
00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:31.082
You do realize
this? I don't care.

653
00:31:31.156 --> 00:31:33.455
I'm not gonna admit to
something that I didn't do!

654
00:31:33.525 --> 00:31:36.927
Okay. I believe you. I believe
you. But I watched that tape.

655
00:31:36.995 --> 00:31:40.693
And as your attorney. I am
begging you. take the deal.

656
00:31:40.766 --> 00:31:42.496
Don't take the deal.

657
00:31:42.968 --> 00:31:44.300
What are you doing?

658
00:31:44.369 --> 00:31:45.546
You're supposed
to be on my side.

659
00:31:45.570 --> 00:31:47.562
Hornstock. I am on your side.

660
00:31:47.639 --> 00:31:50.040
I mean. not technically.
because of the shape of this table.

661
00:31:50.108 --> 00:31:53.567
Imagine a round table. I would
have sat somewhere in the middle.

662
00:31:54.579 --> 00:31:57.743
Okay. tomorrow morning
when the jury watches this tape.

663
00:31:57.816 --> 00:32:00.183
we will lose this case.

664
00:32:00.252 --> 00:32:03.916
This tape is not telling us
the whole truth. There's more.

665
00:32:03.989 --> 00:32:07.357
I need to take this tape. You just
work on your closing arguments.

666
00:32:07.426 --> 00:32:08.724
You leave the rest to me.

667
00:32:11.163 --> 00:32:12.907
Quit pacing. Shawn.
You're making me nervous.

668
00:32:12.931 --> 00:32:13.955
I can't afford it. Dad.

669
00:32:14.032 --> 00:32:17.298
I can't afford a guilty verdict
on my record right now. I can't!

670
00:32:17.369 --> 00:32:20.396
You do realize that you're
not a real lawyer? Right?

671
00:32:20.472 --> 00:32:22.270
You don't have a record.

672
00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:24.485
It's so weird. The prosecution
keeps treating this case

673
00:32:24.509 --> 00:32:26.341
like a crime of passion. right?

674
00:32:26.411 --> 00:32:27.688
But she only knew him
for a couple of hours.

675
00:32:27.712 --> 00:32:31.649
I ask you. how much passion can you
muster up for someone in a couple of hours?

676
00:32:31.716 --> 00:32:35.175
Yeah. well. crimes of passion
are rarely about love or sex. Shawn.

677
00:32:35.253 --> 00:32:38.519
They're closer to
revenge. sometimes hatred.

678
00:32:38.924 --> 00:32:41.223
I would say that your
angry meteorologist

679
00:32:41.293 --> 00:32:42.989
is the best suspect
you got going.

680
00:32:43.061 --> 00:32:44.893
He didn't do it. Yeah.
I know that. Shawn.

681
00:32:44.963 --> 00:32:48.422
The point is you need to find
somebody who felt like that.

682
00:32:48.500 --> 00:32:51.446
Oh. Dad. believe me. there are plenty.
The guy slept with half of Santa Barbara.

683
00:32:51.470 --> 00:32:55.066
We put them all on the stand. The problem is
that Sandra is the only one who was there.

684
00:32:55.140 --> 00:32:57.132
You have a whisk. I do.

685
00:32:57.209 --> 00:32:59.235
And you're not
looking close enough.

686
00:32:59.311 --> 00:33:00.540
Well. you know what?

687
00:33:00.612 --> 00:33:04.140
It's tough. when virtually everything
imaginable is stacked against me.

688
00:33:04.216 --> 00:33:06.276
I've got your ass staring
me down in the courtroom.

689
00:33:06.351 --> 00:33:09.082
I've got a defense attorney who
breaks every time the wind blows.

690
00:33:09.154 --> 00:33:11.299
I've got to hitch rides every
time I need to go somewhere

691
00:33:11.323 --> 00:33:14.657
because. get this. there's some
rogue meter maid who's decided to have

692
00:33:14.726 --> 00:33:16.686
a ticketing vendetta against
me and my motorcycle.

693
00:33:16.728 --> 00:33:19.207
Well. Shawn. maybe that might
not happen if you didn't park your bike

694
00:33:19.231 --> 00:33:21.666
14 feet from a fire hydrant
outside your apartment.

695
00:33:21.733 --> 00:33:24.862
Dad. you've seen my street.
The parking is a joke and...

696
00:33:27.239 --> 00:33:28.798
How did you know that?

697
00:33:31.610 --> 00:33:34.375
Whoa. whoa. whoa. How did you
know that? Wait a second. How...

698
00:33:34.446 --> 00:33:36.847
How do you know that?

699
00:33:36.915 --> 00:33:39.612
Oh. look who's
paying attention now?

700
00:33:39.818 --> 00:33:43.152
You tipped them off? You
tipped them off about my bike?

701
00:33:43.221 --> 00:33:45.122
Who taught you
how to drive. Shawn?

702
00:33:45.190 --> 00:33:48.683
Who do you represent every
time you're out on that road?

703
00:33:48.760 --> 00:33:52.128
I don't represent anybody
when I go out on the road!

704
00:33:52.597 --> 00:33:54.429
Dad. they took my bike!

705
00:33:54.499 --> 00:33:55.694
Tell it to the embassy.

706
00:33:55.767 --> 00:33:58.212
